//
// A HOLE BEHIND A NESTED PATTERN IS NAMED BY ITS OUTER VARIANT (`@FR-M-Exhaust` crossed with
// `@FR-M-Total`).  M-Total: `total(V{f…})` holds only when every field sub-pattern is total, so
// the two `Node` arms — one asking both children to be `Leaf`, one asking the left to be a
// `Node` — leave `Node { l: Leaf, r: Node }` uncovered, and `Node` does not count as covered.
// M-Exhaust then refuses the match, naming the variant whose arms are not total: `Node`, the
// outer variant, not the uncovered shape inside it.  That is the contract today (the OCaml
// bar's C6 reads PARTIAL for it); a sharper message is a change to this cell.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: match on T is not exhaustive — missing: Node
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 9121f1b50, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the outer variant.
// HOLDS: `a-hole-in-a-token-match-names-the-missing-variants` beside it.

enum T { Leaf, Node { l: reference<T>, r: reference<T> } }

fn f(t: T) -> integer {
  match t {
    Leaf => 0,
    Node { l: Leaf, r: Leaf } => 1,
    Node { l: Node { l, r }, r: _ } => 2,
  }
}

fn main() {
  assert(f(Leaf) == 0, "unreachable");
}
